    <class name="Block"
           c:symbol-prefix="block"
           c:type="DexBlock"
           parent="Future"
           final="1"
           glib:type-name="DexBlock"
           glib:get-type="dex_block_get_type"
           glib:fundamental="1">
      <doc xml:space="preserve"
           filename="src/dex-block.c"
           line="28">`DexBlock` represents a callback thunk that can be scheduled to run
within a specific [struct@GLib.MainContext].

You create these by chaining futures together using [ctor@Dex.Future.then],
[ctor@Dex.Future.catch], [ctor@Dex.Future.finally] and similar.

Callback data destruction is queued on the captured scheduler, including when
the block is discarded before invocation. It may run after future completion.</doc>
      <method name="get_kind" c:identifier="dex_block_get_kind">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="src/dex-block.c"
             line="296">Gets the kind of block.

The kind of block relates to what situations the block would be
executed such as for handling a future resolution, rejection, or
both.</doc>
        <source-position filename="src/dex-block.h" line="52"/>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="none">
          <doc xml:space="preserve"
               filename="src/dex-block.c"
               line="306">the [enum@Dex.BlockKind] associated with the @block</doc>
          <type name="BlockKind" c:type="DexBlockKind"/>
        </return-value>
        <parameters>
          <instance-parameter name="block" transfer-ownership="none">
            <doc xml:space="preserve"
                 filename="src/dex-block.c"
                 line="298">a [class@Dex.Block]</doc>
            <type name="Block" c:type="DexBlock*"/>
          </instance-parameter>
        </parameters>
      </method>
      <method name="get_scheduler" c:identifier="dex_block_get_scheduler">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="src/dex-block.c"
             line="316">Gets the scheduler to use when executing a block.</doc>
        <source-position filename="src/dex-block.h" line="54"/>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="none">
          <doc xml:space="preserve"
               filename="src/dex-block.c"
               line="322">the [class@Dex.Scheduler] associated with the @block</doc>
          <type name="Scheduler" c:type="DexScheduler*"/>
        </return-value>
        <parameters>
          <instance-parameter name="block" transfer-ownership="none">
            <doc xml:space="preserve"
                 filename="src/dex-block.c"
                 line="318">a [class@Dex.Block]</doc>
            <type name="Block" c:type="DexBlock*"/>
          </instance-parameter>
        </parameters>
      </method>
    </class>
