      <constructor name="new_fiber"
                   c:identifier="dex_generator_new_fiber"
                   version="1.3">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="src/dex-generator.c"
             line="701">Creates a lazy fiber producer. The first pull starts the fiber; each yield
waits for another pull. A successful final future means exhaustion, and a
rejected final future means failure. Returning %NULL retains the normal fiber
error. If no thread scheduler exists, the process default is captured.</doc>
