      <method name="build"
              c:identifier="dex_graph_builder_build"
              version="1.3"
              throws="1">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="src/dex-graph.c"
             line="340">Validates the dependency graph and creates a future that starts its ready
operations when observed. Each operation runs once, after all of its
dependencies resolve. A rejected dependency prevents its dependents from
starting. The graph resolves after every operation resolves, and rejects
if any operation rejects.

A successful build consumes the nodes from @builder. The builder may then
be freed. Node handles are only used while configuring the builder.</doc>
        <source-position filename="src/dex-graph.h" line="45"/>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="full" nullable="1">
          <doc xml:space="preserve"
               filename="src/dex-graph.c"
               line="354">the graph future, or %NULL on a cycle</doc>
          <type name="Future" c:type="DexFuture*"/>
