        <return-value transfer-ownership="none">
          <doc xml:space="preserve"
               filename="src/dex-state-machine.c"
               line="883">%TRUE if an active transition context was marked interrupted;
  otherwise %FALSE</doc>
          <type name="gboolean" c:type="gboolean"/>
        </return-value>
        <parameters>
          <instance-parameter name="state_machine" transfer-ownership="none">
            <doc xml:space="preserve"
                 filename="src/dex-state-machine.c"
                 line="874">a [class@Dex.StateMachine]</doc>
            <type name="StateMachine" c:type="DexStateMachine*"/>
          </instance-parameter>
        </parameters>
      </method>
      <method name="transition" c:identifier="dex_state_machine_transition">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="src/dex-state-machine.c"
             line="785">Requests a transition to @target.

If @target is a valid value for the state machine's enum type, it becomes
the requested state immediately and can be read with
[method@Dex.StateMachine.get_requested_state]. The requested state is the
most recent valid target passed to this method. It may differ from the
current state and does not imply that the transition will succeed.

Transition requests are serialized. The matching callback is run from a
fiber and may use `dex_await()` to wait for asynchronous work. If the
callback succeeds without calling
[method@Dex.StateTransitionContext.set_state], the state machine commits
@target. If the callback updates the state directly, the returned future
resolves to the current state after the callback returns.</doc>
        <source-position filename="src/dex-state-machine.h" line="108"/>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="full">
          <doc xml:space="preserve"
               filename="src/dex-state-machine.c"
               line="805">a future resolving to the final enum state</doc>
          <type name="Future" c:type="DexFuture*"/>
        </return-value>
        <parameters>
          <instance-parameter name="state_machine" transfer-ownership="none">
            <doc xml:space="preserve"
                 filename="src/dex-state-machine.c"
                 line="787">a [class@Dex.StateMachine]</doc>
            <type name="StateMachine" c:type="DexStateMachine*"/>
          </instance-parameter>
          <parameter name="target" transfer-ownership="none">
            <doc xml:space="preserve"
                 filename="src/dex-state-machine.c"
                 line="788">the target state</doc>
            <type name="guint" c:type="guint"/>
          </parameter>
        </parameters>
      </method>
