      <method name="submit"
              c:identifier="dex_thread_pool_submit"
              version="1.2">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="src/dex-thread-pool.c"
             line="275">Queues blocking work to run on one of the pool's reusable threads.

Callback data is freed on the submitting thread's scheduler, or the default
scheduler if there is none. This may happen after the future completes.

The provided @thread_name is applied to the returned future using
`dex_future_set_static_name()` so that tracing and debugging tools can
identify the work item. It does not rename the underlying OS worker thread.</doc>
        <source-position filename="src/dex-thread-pool.h" line="52"/>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="full">
          <doc xml:space="preserve"
               filename="src/dex-thread-pool.c"
               line="292">a future that resolves when the work completes</doc>
