    </function>
    <function name="aio_open" c:identifier="dex_aio_open" version="1.2">
      <doc xml:space="preserve"
           filename="src/dex-aio.c"
           line="73">An asynchronous `open()` wrapper.

Generally you want to provide `NULL` for the @aio_context as that
will get the default aio context for your scheduler.

The resulting future resolves to a file descriptor which can be consumed
with [method@Dex.Future.await_fd]. If the file descriptor is not consumed,
it is closed asynchronously when the result is freed.</doc>
      <source-position filename="src/dex-aio.h" line="34"/>
      <return-value transfer-ownership="full">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="src/dex-aio.c"
             line="89">a future that will resolve when the
  open completes or rejects with error.</doc>
        <type name="Future" c:type="DexFuture*"/>
      </return-value>
      <parameters>
        <parameter name="aio_context"
                   transfer-ownership="none"
                   nullable="1"
                   allow-none="1">
          <type name="AioContext" c:type="DexAioContext*"/>
        </parameter>
        <parameter name="path" transfer-ownership="none">
          <doc xml:space="preserve"
               filename="src/dex-aio.c"
               line="76">the path to open</doc>
